  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Leading a United Pathway to Anti-Trafficking Action (LUPTA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to advance and contribute to the Romanian Government&#x2019;s endeavors in successfully implementing Romania&#x2019;s National Strategy for 2018-2022 and National Action Plan for Combating Trafficking in Persons. Of particular focus will be developing and implementing a multi-disciplinary, holistic, systematized victim centered approach to human trafficking investigations and prosecutions based on a collaboration protocol on coordination of victims of trafficking in the criminal procedure. This will incorporate internationally accepted best practices and guidelines, and bring together all actors involved in the investigation, prosecution, protection, and public and/or public support services provided for victims of trafficking. The project aims to increase and improve the knowledge, skills, practices, and capacity of targeted key actors, introducing interdisciplinary expertise and innovative judicial tools to build specialized counter-trafficking competency within the Romanian law enforcement and criminal justice sector. Furthermore, the project will address needed improvements to victim protection and increase victim participation in the criminal justice process.</narrative>
  </description>
